# Level 25, reached by password GYLM, and the boss fought in the corridor it
# actually crosses rather than wherever the player happened to be standing.
#
# **The previous round fired 596 shots at this boss for one point of damage and
# concluded that it does not walk into a stream of fire. There was no stream of
# fire.** Every shot died six pixels from the barrel. Sampled per frame instead
# of every fourth -- the fire rate is 12 frames, so the old every-fourth sampling
# aliased against it and always caught a shot at the same age -- a shot spawns at
# x=665, reaches x=671, and is gone. That is the same two-frame, six-pixel death
# that proved level 17's creature was in a sealed pen rather than behind an uncut
# route. `movies/level25-heavy.zmv` and all four parked experiments stood at
# y=561, pressed against the wall that bounds the corridor, shooting into it.
#
# `zamn_assets route --reach <rom> 26` puts that corridor at **y=588 and 408
# pixels long**, running straight through the band the boss spends about 40% of
# its time in. Twenty-seven pixels lower and the same gun works.
#
# Two changes from `level25-heavy`, and no new route:
#
#  * **Fire is held from frame 3387**, the second $22 pickup. That movie spends
#    all forty $67 shots -- four damage each, and not one of the four ids this
#    boss rewrites -- walking north with Y held down, at about ten percent. Here
#    they survive the trip, so the fight starts with the boss on its full 70.
#  * The tail sweeps the lane in 300-frame legs instead of spinning on the spot.
#
# **70 -> 44.** Twenty-six damage against the recorded movie's sixteen, and the
# first number in this fight that came from aiming the experiment rather than
# from lengthening it.
#
# `boss_died` is still untaken. The reachable arsenal is 390 damage of
# ammunition -- 150 $5C, 40 $67, 20 $61 rewritten to $60 -- against 70 of health,
# and the lane has not yet held better than a fifth of it. The three weapons that
# would settle it are all off the boss's side of the map: $5F's 300 shots and $64
# sit inside scenery, and $62 is in a sealed pocket. See docs/cosim.md, "The
# stream of fire that was a wall".
